      "devdoc": {
        "details": "Each OnchainApp constructor verifies its own bytes. The directory snapshots      their hashes and lengths; clients MUST verify the complete compressed and      expanded hashes before executing. This contract never assembles the full      resource in one call. Shard implementations are supplied by the deployer;      a dishonest/unavailable shard can prevent retrieval, never bypass a digest.",
        "kind": "dev",
